WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:08.029
This very moment of time and space is occupied
by everything that exists.

00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:11.930
You, me, and everything in between.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:18.460
We are all experiencing this same moment,
and we are all experiencing this same moment

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.460
differently.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:27.070
Even if you and I were to look out the exact
same window at the exact same street at the

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:35.620
exact same time, it is likely that we would
both see and experience something different.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:41.960
Perhaps you might enjoy watching all the people
walk by and musingly ponder about where they

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.530
could all be coming from and where they could
all be going.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:52.719
And perhaps, I might look at all the traffic
and become tense with anticipation of the

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:58.570
chaos that I will be faced with when going
outside to commute somewhere.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:04.080
Or perhaps you see the latter and I see the
former.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:10.990
Regardless, it is likely that we both have
two different mental experiences of the same

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:14.340
thing at the same time.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.380
But how is this possible?

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:23.740
How can we live on the same planet, sharing
the same reality, looking at the same objects,

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:28.450
yet all have different experiences?

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:31.909
We all have uniquely coded DNA.

00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:41.460
And we all have unique pasts with unique upbringings,
influences, and environmental conditions.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:47.810
All of these factors, and perhaps some others,
work together to form the lens out of which

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:53.579
we see the world and experience the life that
engulfs us.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:59.100
And it is this lens that we form our self-identity
out of.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:03.340
How we view and feel about things is all we
know.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:10.310
It is our truth, and for our truth and identity
to be challenged is to feel the existential

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:13.640
sting of a thousand bees.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:18.360
And as a result, everyone has something to
say about everything.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:21.830
And everyone likes to think that they are
right.

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:27.810
But yet, we are often all saying different
and conflicting things.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:34.030
And so perhaps sometimes, just because we
know we are right, does not always mean that

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:36.320
we are.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:44.110
Amidst the world, there are countless ideologies,
philosophies, and perspectives that simultaneously

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:48.320
exist in direct conflict with each another.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:56.380
There is Catholicism and atheism, monism and
dualism, nihilism and existentialism, and

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:04.840
endless more, all very different yet equally
as real and true to those who behold them.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:11.870
The spectrum of ideologies in life is unending
and overwhelming.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.470
What is the right one?

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:15.330
How do we know?

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:16.990
Can we know?

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:21.750
And if not, should we even subscribe to anything
at all?

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:28.870
In general, an ideology is simply a system
of beliefs and theories on how to live or

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:29.870
function.

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:31.420
But that is it.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:39.510
And problems arise when we let our identity
and ego become so deeply engrained in a particular

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:45.800
ideology that we neglect to remember that
that is all it is.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:49.210
That it is not a rigid and universal fact
of life.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:57.940
It is just ideas, theories, and principles
constructed in an attempt to combat the inexorable

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:02.940
uncertainty and complexity of human life.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:09.020
Truthfully, we are all in conflict with understanding
the life around us.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:15.920
And when forming our beliefs and perspectives,
our goal should not be to subscribe permanently

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:24.190
and exclusively to something that sets limitations
for our self or others regarding what we can

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.939
experience, believe, and consider.

00:04:26.939 --> 00:04:31.279
There is no universally correct ideology.

00:04:31.279 --> 00:04:37.210
Perhaps there are some that consistently hit
closer to the sweet spot of common sense,

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:41.999
but there is currently no one-size-fits-all.

00:04:41.999 --> 00:04:47.889
There are too many variances in the nature
and nurture of individuals for everyone to

00:04:47.889 --> 00:04:56.820
agree on one ideology, and life is to complex
for one ideology to apply to every facet of

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:57.820
life.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:05.029
If life is complex and constantly in flux,
so should we be, along with our beliefs and

00:05:05.029 --> 00:05:07.379
perspectives.

00:05:07.379 --> 00:05:13.090
True intelligence comes with the admission
of ignorance and the admission of our incomplete

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:17.740
pursuit of knowledge and understanding.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:24.430
Intelligence is to engage in discussion with
other opinions, ideas, and perspectives and

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:29.550
consider them for what they are with openness
and reason.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:36.229
If we want truth, we must be willing to pull
from varying ideologies, however dogmatically

00:05:36.229 --> 00:05:39.129
contradictory they may be.

00:05:39.129 --> 00:05:46.419
We must be able to consider individual concepts
and issues for what they are, using a combination

00:05:46.419 --> 00:05:56.180
of scientific understanding, empirical evidence,
self-knowledge, personal reflection, and reason.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:03.910
And we must do so, not seeking to see if they
fit within our existing beliefs and ideologies,

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:09.740
but to simply find the most accurate and applicable
answers to our questions.

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:17.069
To move fluidly with life and not get left
behind in our stalls of expired self-righteousness.

